legend bottom
  <b>Reading the map</b>
  Box colours match the node types on the Knowledge Graph page.
  <b>stream</b> and <b>system</b> are a fixed vocabulary, hard-coded in the extractor —
  a platform absent from that list gets no node, however often documents name it.
  Solid arrows start at a document; <b>subprocess_of</b> is the only relation between
  two nodes of the same type, and alone is derived, looked up in the BPML hierarchy.
  Every document relationship carries its evidence: the rule that made it, how often
  the target is named, and the chunks that name it.
  Dashed arrows are the passage layer: <b>(:Chunk)-[:MENTIONS]->(entity)</b>.
  Two systems are connected only through a document naming both — any longer
  route runs via a stream, which is co-membership, not an integration.
end legend

@enduml
